\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Launch structure of the fused kernel (Section~\ref {sec:impl:fused}). Each block computes one stream's row sums entirely in shared memory, contributes exact atomic sums to the global fine powers (and, when bound, the debug taps), and increments a per-frame completion counter folded into the mask word; the last-arriving block re-reads the finalized sums and executes the exact decision arithmetic, overwriting the counter with the mask bit. Blue boxes are the only global-memory traffic.}}{57}{figure.6.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fused}{{6.1}{57}{Launch structure of the fused kernel (Section~\ref {sec:impl:fused}). Each block computes one stream's row sums entirely in shared memory, contributes exact atomic sums to the global fine powers (and, when bound, the debug taps), and increments a per-frame completion counter folded into the mask word; the last-arriving block re-reads the finalized sums and executes the exact decision arithmetic, overwriting the counter with the mask bit. Blue boxes are the only global-memory traffic}{figure.6.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Legacy paired implementation-loss measurement. The entries are the horizontal difference between the full-precision and packed-\texttt  {int4} crossings on the same trials; negative values indicate that the packed crossing was slightly more favorable. These are measurements of the earlier $512$-row, coarse-statistic geometry, not of the present two-stage detector.}}{58}{table.6.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:impl:legacyloss}{{6.1}{58}{Legacy paired implementation-loss measurement. The entries are the horizontal difference between the full-precision and packed-\texttt {int4} crossings on the same trials; negative values indicate that the packed crossing was slightly more favorable. These are measurements of the earlier $512$-row, coarse-statistic geometry, not of the present two-stage detector}{table.6.1}{}}
